		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4350&amp;p=32705#p32705"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi,<br><br>The RD-5R has an EEPROM, so there is no "extra" space on the GD77, or any supported radio (BTW, the firmware isn't located in the external Flash chip, but in the MCU).<br>The STM32 based radios don't have EEPROM.<br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel</div></blockquote>Thank you Daniel, So, bacically, both RD-5R and GD77 have the same memory structure.<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>The MK22's "NMEA" versions are supporting the NMEA logging, but it does impact the flash memory storage space (Voice and/or DMRID storage), as you need some space to store that NMEA sentences.<br>So, if you don't have made any GPS module mod, and not interested in related logging, you can safely ignore such firmware builds.</div></blockquote>I might want to do the GPS mod in the future. Is it save to say, If I get the GPS mod done I will then need the NMEA version of the firmware?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Sun Sep 01, 2024 12:51 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
