		<author><name><![CDATA[F1RMB]]></name></author>
		<updated>2024-09-01T08:20:39</updated>

		<published>2024-09-01T08:20:39</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4350&amp;p=32698#p32698</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4350&amp;p=32698#p32698"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Open box GD-77's available from Radioddity]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4350&amp;p=32698#p32698"><![CDATA[
The MK22's "NMEA" versions are supporting the NMEA logging, but it does impact the flash memory storage space (Voice and/or DMRID storage), as you need some space to store that NMEA sentences.<br>So, if you don't have made any GPS module mod, and not interested in related logging, you can safely ignore such firmware builds.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sun Sep 01, 2024 8:20 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
